Schemas

.blueprint of my DB 
.defines:
    .what tables exist
    .what columns exist in each table
    .what data types each column has
    .what relationships exist between tables
    .what constraints exist on the data (e.g. primary keys, foreign keys, unique constraints, etc.)
.its the foundation for designing and implementing a database


How schema connects to the rest of the system:
.user belongs to many conversations
.conversation can have many users
.message belongs to a conversation
.conversation has many messages
.user has many messages through conversations


